      "id": 153477,
      "name": "Dandolo",
      "username": "Dandolo",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dandolo/{size}/1845_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-11T00:59:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I played a game where a Shinobi was the top card of Mr. Fixer's deck when he was incapped. Later we wanted to revive him with Rites of Revival but we had no idea what that meant for the Shinobi! &nbsp;We wound up reviving Setback for the third time instead.... really interesting game. &nbsp;Anyway, was wondering how everyone thought this would work. &nbsp;Also when Fixer was incapped we played it that his cards were removed from play but the Shinobi stayed put, remaining the top (and only) card of his deck... does anyone disagree with that interpretation?</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:32:49.437Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
