    {
      "id": 153479,
      "name": "Ronway",
      "username": "Ronway",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-11T01:13:05.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm actually not sure what happens to a Shinobi that is on top of a hero deck.</p><p>For starters the Rulebook's glossary has this to say about incapacitation</p><blockquote><p>A Hero is incapacitated when reduced to 0 or fewer HP. When this occurs, immediately remove all of that hero's cards from the game and flip the Hero Character Card.</p></blockquote><p>Since the Shinobi is not one of their cards, the card would not be removed from the game. So my best guess is that it would remain where there. I guess cards like Fumbling Fool could discard it, thus putting it back into play. That would then allow the arguement of allowing other Shinobi to be stacked ontop of it.</p><p>If I were playing and this occured, I would just have it go back into play in the Environment play area.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:32:49.577Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
